<h2 id="ctodo-workflow" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. Workflow</h2>

On **`ctodo <description>`**:

1. **Bootstrap** — ensure `docs_manual_gen/todos/` and `TODO_IDEAS_LIST.md` exist ([§2](#ctodo-bootstrap)).
2. **Parse** — extract idea text; derive a **title** (short headline) and **slug** (`kebab-case`, ASCII, max ~48 chars).
3. **Dedupe** — if an entry with the same **`slug:`** already exists, **update that entry**; else **append** a new entry ([§5](#ctodo-dedupe)).
4. **Analyze** — produce structured analysis from the description ([§4](#ctodo-analysis)).
5. **Write** — merge into `TODO_IDEAS_LIST.md`; set **`last-modified`** to today (ISO date); on new entries set **`added`** to today and **`status: new`** unless facts imply otherwise ([§3](#ctodo-entry)).
6. **Reply briefly** — confirm ID, title, status, and path; do not dump the full file unless asked.

**Out of scope for `ctodo` alone:** implementing code or creating plan files — unless the user also asks. Linking to plans is a **metadata update** when status becomes `planned`.

