<h2 id="ctodo-analysis" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Analysis content</h2>

Analysis must be **clean and scannable** — not a raw chat dump. Infer reasonably from the description; label uncertainty in **open questions**. Do not invent repo files; if linking plans or code, **grep or read** first.

If the user’s text clearly says work is already in a plan or already shipped, set **`status`** to **`planned`** or **`d-impl`** accordingly on first write or update.

---

<h2 id="ctodo-dedupe" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Update vs append</h2>

- **Same `slug`** in an existing entry → **update** that section: refresh analysis, **`last-modified`**, status/plans if changed; **preserve `id` and `added`**.
- **New slug** → **append** new **`###`** block with next **`CTODO-NNN`**.
- **Slug change** for same idea → treat as new entry unless user asks to merge; optionally note superseded id in **open questions**.

**Anchor ids:** heading **`id="ctodo-NNN-slug"`** must match **`id`** and **`slug`** for outline links.
